CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ a < b: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ !\(b < a\): SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
no comparison operator
--
Fixed: cbmc reported "no comparison operator for an operand of class type
'struct iter'": the hidden friend's return type named T, the enclosing
class template's parameter, which was unbound once the friend was hoisted
to the namespace ("symbol 'T' is unknown").  With libstdc++ 16,
std::string::iterator was not random_access_iterator because of this,
and _Seq_sink::_M_reserve and _M_span of <format> lost their bodies.
Reduced from that with cvise (g++ 16 as the validity check).
